$CATEGORY: Vocabulary/HansenQuinn/4-ppm-01

::Q001::[markdown]muse:{
	~%-100%γῆ, γῆς, ἡ#Incorrect. **γῆ, γῆς, ἡ** means “earth” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%νύξ, νυκτός, ἡ#Incorrect. **νύξ, νυκτός, ἡ** means “night” (Chapter 6).
	~%-100%ὕδωρ, ὕδατος, τό#Incorrect. **ὕδωρ, ὕδατος, τό** means “water” (Chapter 9).
	~%-100%ἀγορά, ἀγορᾶς, ἡ#Incorrect. **ἀγορά, ἀγορᾶς, ἡ** means “market place” (Chapter 1).
	~%100%μοῦσα, μούσης, ἡ#Correct: **μοῦσα, μούσης, ἡ** → “muse” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ἄργυρος, ἄργυρου, ὁ#Incorrect. **ἄργυρος, ἄργυρου, ὁ** means “silver” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%θάλαττα, θαλάττης, ἡ#Incorrect. **θάλαττα, θαλάττης, ἡ** means “sea” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%θεός, ὁ#Incorrect. **θεός, ὁ** means “god” (Chapter 1).
}


::Q002::[markdown]worthy of ( + gen.):{
	~%-100%μακρός, μακρά, μακρόν#Incorrect. **μακρός, μακρά, μακρόν** means “large” (Chapter 5).
	~%100%ἄξιος, ἀξίᾱ, ἄξιον#Correct: **ἄξιος, ἀξίᾱ, ἄξιον** → “worthy of ( + gen.)” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%φοβερός, φοβερά, φοβερόν#Incorrect. **φοβερός, φοβερά, φοβερόν** means “fearful” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%πας, πασα, παν#Incorrect. **πας, πασα, παν** means “all, every” (Chapter 8).
	~%-100%ἐχθρός, ἐχθρά, ἐχθρόν#Incorrect. **ἐχθρός, ἐχθρά, ἐχθρόν** means “hated” (Chapter 9).
	~%-100%ἄλογος, ἄλογον#Incorrect. **ἄλογος, ἄλογον** means “unreasonable” (Chapter 9).
	~%-100%ἀλεθής, ἀληθές#Incorrect. **ἀλεθής, ἀληθές** means “true” (Chapter 10).
	~%-100%αἴτιος αἰτία αἴτιον#Incorrect. **αἴτιος αἰτία αἴτιον** means “responsible (for) + gen.” (Chapter 11).
}


::Q003::[markdown]wish:{
	~%-100%ἦρχα#Incorrect. **ἦρχα** is Principal Part 4 of **ἄρχω** “rule” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%κεχόρευμαι#Incorrect. **κεχόρευμαι** is Principal Part 5 of **χορεύω** “dance” (Chapter 6).
	~%100%ἠθέληκα#Correct: **ἠθέληκα** is Principal Part 4 of **ἐθέλω** “wish” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%πέπεισμαι#Incorrect. **πέπεισμαι** is Principal Part 5 of **πείθω** “persuade” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%ἠξίωσα#Incorrect. **ἠξίωσα** is Principal Part 3 of **ἀξιόω** “think worthy of” (Chapter 10).
	~%-100%πείθω#Incorrect. **πείθω** is Principal Part 1 of **πείθω** “persuade” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%ἔθαψα#Incorrect. **ἔθαψα** is Principal Part 3 of **θάπτω** “bury” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%ἀκούσομαι#Incorrect. **ἀκούσομαι** is Principal Part 2 of **ἀκούω** “hear (+ acc. of thing)” (Chapter 11).
}


::Q004::[markdown]Which Principal Part is the ‘Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’?:{
	~%-100%3rd#Incorrect. ‘Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **4th Principal Part**, not the 3rd.
	~%-100%5th#Incorrect. ‘Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **4th Principal Part**, not the 5th.
	~%-100%6th#Incorrect. ‘Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **4th Principal Part**, not the 6th.
	~%-100%1st#Incorrect. ‘Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **4th Principal Part**, not the 1st.
	~%100%4th#Correct: ‘Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **4th Principal Part**.
	~%-100%2nd#Incorrect. ‘Perfect, Active, Indicative, 1st person, Singular’ is the **4th Principal Part**, not the 2nd.
}


